  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mustafa Muhammed vs Muvattupuzha Municipality on 13 December, 2024 Wp(C) No.44563/2024 1/4 Order Date : 13-12-2 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr.Justice Ziyad Rahman A.A. Friday, the 13th day of December 2024 / 22nd Agrahayana, 1946 Wp(C) No. 44563 Of 2024 Petitioner: Mustafa Muhammed, Aged 63 Years S/O. Muhammed Hanif, Residing At Thaze Nanoth House, Koorara P O, Mokeri, Kannur, Pin - 670694 Respondent: 1. Muvattupuzha Municipality, Municipal Office, Muvattupuzha Old Bridge Road,Thottummalpeedika, Muvattupuzha, Ernakulam District Rep. By Its Secretary, Pin - 686673 2. The Secretary, Muvattupuzha Municipality,Municipal Office, Muvattupuzha Old Bridge Road,Thottummalpeedika, Muvattupuzha, Ernakulam District, Pin - 686673 3. The District Transport Officer, Kerala State Road Transport Corporation,Muvattupuzha P O, Ernakulam District, Pin - 686673 Writ petition (civil) praying inter alia that in the circumstances stated in the affidavit filed along with the Wp(C) the High Court be pleased to direct the 1st respondent to permit the petitioner to continue the tea shop established in the kerala state road transport corporation bus station, muvattuppuzha based on ext p1 agreement and ext p2 extension order, pending disposal of the above writ petition.",
    "facts": "3. Considering the fact that, the petitioner herein is conducting a tea shop on the basis of Ext.P1 agreement executed between the petitioner and the KSRTC and also that, the petitioner has obtained Ext.P4 from the Department of Industries and Commerce, under Kerala Micro Small Medium Enterprises Facilitation Rules, 2020 to set up a service enterprise, I am inclined to pass an interim order. Moreover, the petitioner has also obtained Ext.P5 license from the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India as well. Besides, it is an undisputed fact that the petitioner has been conducting the shop since 2022.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
